===== PinnedPurgeDisclosure
{ "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "required": [ "runId", "activePins", "consequences" ], "description": "Complete current pin inventory observed under the purge writer lease. Operational pinId is a host-ledger name scoped to this Run, not a content identity or authority token. Never truncate this disclosure or infer destructive consent from it.", "properties": { "runId": { "$ref": "#/$defs/RunId" }, "activePins": { "type": "array", "minItems": 1, "maxItems": 4096, "x-opensip-order": { "by": [ "pinId" ] }, "items": { "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "required": [ "pinId", "kind" ], "properties": { "pinId": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 256 }, "kind": { "type": "string", "enum": [ "baseline", "repair-prerequisite", "backup-export", "other-authorized" ] } } } }, "consequences": { "type": "array", "const": [ "named-pins-revoked", "dependent-evidence-replay-unavailable", "sealed-history-retained" ], "items": { "type": "string" }, "x-opensip-order": "sequence" } } }
===== CapabilityAvailabilityV1
{ "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "required": [ "stepCount", "totalNoticeCount", "steps" ], "properties": { "stepCount": { "$ref": "#/$defs/Uint53" }, "totalNoticeCount": { "$ref": "#/$defs/Uint53" }, "steps": { "type": "array", "minItems": 0, "maxItems": 64, "uniqueItems": true, "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/CapabilityAvailabilityStepV1" }, "x-opensip-order": "sequence" } }, "description": "The invocation's availability account, composed PER STEP. An earlier revision used one flat array bounded at 1024 and argued it could not truncate because that is the analysis-spec bound - but 1024 is per analysis-spec, not per invocation, and a named multi-step invocation carries up to 64 steps: two admitted selections of 1023 requests each compose 2046 notices and the flat array refused. Composing per step preserves every valid admitted invocation: each step keeps its own bounded collection, `steps` is bounded by the invocation step bound (StepId 0..63), and no notice is ever discarded to fit. `totalNoticeCount` is the sum of the step counts and is authoritative for a caller counting absences across the invocation. A step that made no selection - a skipped step, or a non-analysis step - contributes NO entry; a step that selected and found nothing absent contributes an entry with an empty array, which is the positive statement that it checked. A retried step keeps ONE entry, for the attempt whose selection the invocation retained." }
===== CapabilityAvailabilityStepV1
{ "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "required": [ "stepId", "noticeCount", "notices" ], "properties": { "stepId": { "$ref": "#/$defs/StepId" }, "noticeCount": { "$ref": "#/$defs/Uint53" }, "notices": { "type": "array", "minItems": 0, "maxItems": 1024, "uniqueItems": true, "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/CapabilityAvailabilityNoticeV1" }, "x-opensip-order": "sequence" } }, "description": "The availability account of ONE analysis step's own selection, associated with that step by stepId. `notices` is bounded at 1024 because that is the analysis-spec requestedCapabilities bound and one selection produces at most one absence per requested row, so a STEP's collection can never truncate and its noticeCount always equals its array length. The same ownership tuple may recur in different steps - two steps may select the same unit - so uniqueness is within a step, never across the invocation." }
===== CapabilityAvailabilityNoticeV1
{ "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "required": [ "code", "capabilityId", "languageMode", "workspaceRoot", "remedy" ], "properties": { "code": { "const": "native.capability-unavailable", "description": "This typed record declares exactly one condition - a capability the selected product requires that this release did not declare available - so its code is that condition, not any DomainDetailCode. An earlier revision referenced the whole enum and admitted CONFIG.INVALID on a release-absence notice." }, "capabilityId": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 128, "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9._:-]*(?![\\s\\S])" }, "languageMode": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 128 }, "workspaceRoot": { "$ref": "#/$defs/UserInputPath" }, "remedy": { "$ref": "#/$defs/BoundedText" } }, "description": "One capability the selected product requires that this release did not declare available, for ONE requested unit. The ownership tuple is carried in TYPED FIELDS - capabilityId, languageMode and the unit's own workspaceRoot - and is never concatenated into `subject`: workspaceRoot is a UserInputPath bounded at 4096 while BoundedText is 1024, so a concatenated subject could silently truncate a path and collapse two distinct requested units into one indistinguishable notice. Advisory: it terminates nothing, mints no Coverage, grants no Control verdict or repair authority, and is never a clone Candidate." }
ENVELOPE: { "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema", "$id": "urn:opensip:product-v1:workflows:command-envelope", "title": "CommandEnvelope major 2 \u2014 explicit successor to the CANDIDATE major-1 union in coop 07 (PROPOSED, revised)", "description": "Discriminated by kind. The four major-1 members retain their meaning; major 2 adds kind=invocation for named workflows and every multi-step invocation, kind=doctor for the diagnostic report, and a mandatory common header carrying the operational RequestId. A single-step builtin command projects its single step's member directly. Consumers pin schemaMajor; an unsupported major is refused with REQUEST.SCHEMA_MAJOR_UNSUPPORTED, never silently reshaped. The JSON envelope is the parity reference: SARIF, HTML and agent renderings must carry semantically equal parity fields, and the agent rendering is this envelope plus advisory hints.", "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "required": [ "schemaFamily", "schemaMajor", "kind", "requestId", "termination", "exitCode" ], "properties": { "schemaFamily": { "const": "opensip.product.envelope" }, "schemaMajor": { "const": 2 }, "kind": { "type": "string", "enum": [ "run", "query", "mutation", "failure", "invocation", "doctor" ] }, "requestId": { "$ref": "urn:opensip:product-v1:workflows:common#/$defs/RequestId" }, "clientCorrelationId": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 128 }, "projectId": { "$ref": "urn:opensip:product-v1:workflows:common#/$defs/ProjectId" }, "projectRoot": { "$ref": "urn:opensip:product-v1:workflows:common#/$defs/UserInputPath" }, "termination": { "$ref": "urn:opensip:product-v1:workflows:common#/$defs/StepTermination" }, "exitCode": { "type": "integer", "enum": [ 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 130 ], "description": "derived from termination.class by the fixed table; the checker refuses any other pairing" }, "run": { "$ref": "urn:opensip:product-v1:workflows:invocation-record#/$defs/AnalysisResult" }, "query": { "$ref": "urn:opensip:pro